# Runtime support floor for Zephyr's WebView targets (NOT open-web population —
# a Tauri app inherits its engine from the host OS, so popularity queries like
# `>0.5%` are meaningless here).
#
#   Windows  -> WebView2 (Chromium)    -> Chrome 110 (toSorted, Feb 2023)
#   Linux    -> WebKitGTK (~Safari)    -> webkit2gtk 4.1 era / Safari 15.4
#   macOS    -> WKWebView (Safari)     -> Safari 15.4 (Monterey)
#
# Nothing in the toolchain consumes this yet (oxlint has no compat rule); it is
# the written-down floor that tsconfig `lib` and the Vite `build.target` mirror.
chrome >= 110
safari >= 15.4
